{
  "slug": "cholesky-decompose",
  "title": "Cholesky Decomposition",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "category": "quant-finance",
  "tags": [
    "quant-finance",
    "linear-algebra",
    "floating-point"
  ],
  "statement": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "md": "A covariance matrix $A$ is symmetric positive definite, so it factors as $A = L L^\\top$ with $L$ lower triangular and positive diagonal. Compute $L$ for an integer matrix $A$."
    },
    {
      "type": "math",
      "tex": "L_{jj} = \\sqrt{A_{jj} - \\sum_{k<j} L_{jk}^2}, \\qquad L_{ij} = \\frac{A_{ij} - \\sum_{k<j} L_{ik} L_{jk}}{L_{jj}} \\;(i > j)"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "md": "Print $L$ as $n$ rows of $n$ numbers (zeros above the diagonal), each with exactly 6 decimals. A value whose absolute size is below $5\\cdot 10^{-7}$ is printed as `0.000000` (never `-0.000000`). The tests keep every printed value away from a rounding tie."
    }
  ],
  "inputFormat": "First line: $n$. Then $n$ lines of $n$ integers: the matrix $A$.",
  "outputFormat": "$n$ lines of $n$ numbers with 6 decimals, separated by single spaces.",
  "constraints": [
    "$1 \\le n \\le 50$",
    "$A$ is symmetric positive definite with $|A_{ij}| \\le 10^6$"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "3\n4 12 -16\n12 37 -43\n-16 -43 98\n",
      "output": "2.000000 0.000000 0.000000\n6.000000 1.000000 0.000000\n-8.000000 5.000000 3.000000\n"
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Process columns left to right; each entry needs only entries already computed.",
    "Clamp tiny values so negative zero is never printed."
  ],
  "editorial": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "md": "The algorithm is $O(n^3)$. Column $j$ of $L$ depends on columns $0..j-1$. For a positive definite matrix the value under the square root is always positive."
    }
  ],
  "lessons": [
    "la-svd-covariance",
    "la-linear-systems"
  ],
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nfrom math import sqrt\n\n\ndef main():\n    tok = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(tok[0])\n    a = [[int(tok[1 + i * n + j]) for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)]\n    L = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for j in range(n):\n        L[j][j] = sqrt(a[j][j] - sum(L[j][k] ** 2 for k in range(j)))\n        for i in range(j + 1, n):\n            L[i][j] = (a[i][j] - sum(L[i][k] * L[j][k] for k in range(j))) / L[j][j]\n    for i in range(n):\n        print(' '.join('0.000000' if abs(x) < 5e-7 else f\"{x:.6f}\" for x in L[i]))\n\n\nmain()",
    "cpp": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &n) != 1) return 1;\n    vector<vector<double>> a(n, vector<double>(n)), L(n, vector<double>(n, 0.0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            long long x;\n            if (scanf(\"%lld\", &x) != 1) return 1;\n            a[i][j] = (double)x;\n        }\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n        double s = a[j][j];\n        for (int k = 0; k < j; k++) s -= L[j][k] * L[j][k];\n        L[j][j] = sqrt(s);\n        for (int i = j + 1; i < n; i++) {\n            double t = a[i][j];\n            for (int k = 0; k < j; k++) t -= L[i][k] * L[j][k];\n            L[i][j] = t / L[j][j];\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (j) putchar(' ');\n            if (fabs(L[i][j]) < 5e-7) printf(\"0.000000\");\n            else printf(\"%.6f\", L[i][j]);\n        }\n        putchar('\\n');\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
  },
